1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:08,150
The brush clears an old bound manuscript, its pages filled with the Vedas. For centuries these were not read.

2
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:15,598
They were recited, and learnt by heart, line by line. The tradition calls them shruti, that which was heard.

3
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:19,121
What is the difference between hearing and remembering?

4
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:38,333
How do we know? This is a story told entirely by texts.

5
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:45,062
The Vedas, the Brahmanas, the Aranyakas and the Upanishads give us ideas, rituals and questions.

6
00:00:45,062 --> 00:00:49,786
The oldest written manuscripts are much later than the words themselves.

7
00:01:02,917 --> 00:01:09,979
There are four Vedas. The Rigveda is a collection of hymns. The Samaveda sets verses to melodies.

8
00:01:09,979 --> 00:01:18,467
The Yajurveda gives the formulas for sacrifice. The Atharvaveda holds spells and healing charms. Each Veda has layers.

9
00:01:18,467 --> 00:01:27,797
The Samhita is the collection of hymns. The Brahmanas explain the rituals. The Aranyakas, the forest texts, move toward meaning.

10
00:01:27,797 --> 00:01:33,819
The Upanishads ask about the self. The word Upanishad means sitting near a teacher.

11
00:01:33,819 --> 00:01:38,821
The Upanishads ask what the self is, and what lies behind the world.

12
00:01:38,821 --> 00:01:42,718
Many scholars see them as the roots of later Indian philosophy.

13
00:01:42,718 --> 00:01:49,304
The national motto, Satyameva Jayate, truth alone triumphs, is taken from the Mundaka Upanishad.

14
00:01:49,304 --> 00:01:55,913
The six Vedangas are the limbs of the Veda: Shiksha, which is sound, Kalpa, which is ritual, Vyakarana,

15
00:01:55,913 --> 00:02:04,098
which is grammar, Nirukta, which is word origins, Chhandas, which is metre, and Jyotisha, which is astronomy.

16
00:02:04,098 --> 00:02:11,572
The epics, the Ramayana and the Mahabharata, belong to a later time. They grew over many centuries.

17
00:02:24,717 --> 00:02:30,169
Old name, new name. The Upanishads are also called Vedanta.

18
00:02:30,169 --> 00:02:38,628
The word means the end of the Veda, because they come at the end of the Vedic texts, and also because they are seen as its highest aim.

19
00:02:51,783 --> 00:03:01,456
Carve this tip into memory. Four Vedas: Rig, Sama, Yajur, Atharva. Hymn, tune, rite, charm.

20
00:03:01,456 --> 00:03:09,145
Four Vedas, four jobs: hymn, tune, rite and charm. Add the Upanishads for philosophy.

21
00:03:22,283 --> 00:03:37,894
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which Veda is a collection of hymns? The answer: the Rigveda. Number two.

22
00:03:37,894 --> 00:03:55,394
Which texts are called the forest books? The answer: the Aranyakas. Number three. Our national motto comes from which Upanishad?

23
00:03:55,394 --> 00:04:01,576
The answer: the Mundaka Upanishad. Now one line for Mains.

24
00:04:01,576 --> 00:04:07,250
Discuss the significance of Vedic literature in understanding ancient Indian society.

25
00:04:24,383 --> 00:04:32,456
The manuscript goes into its case. It holds words that were remembered for centuries. Three facts to take away.

26
00:04:32,456 --> 00:04:40,720
Four Vedas and their later layers. Shruti: learnt by ear, not by eye. Upanishads ask about the self.

27
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:44,681
Next gallery: Sixteen Mahajanapadas.

